{#
  RAIL — Figma 911:530. The page's left menu, one item per section. The
  logo moved out of it and now follows the name in the intro (1155:10691).

  STICKY FOR THE WHOLE PAGE. It sits in .v4-rail-track, a full-height column
  down the left of .v4-shell, and sticks inside it; the header's left gutter is
  left empty so the rail starts exactly where the comp draws it (x=40, y=132).

  IT NEVER COVERS CONTENT. Nothing else on the page may enter the rail's column
  (--v4-rail-clear). The project strips, which in the comp run from x=40, start
  past it instead; see _work.css.

  scripts/v4-rail.js moves .is-active / aria-current to the item whose section
  is under the top of the viewport. Without JS the first item stays active.

  ITEMS. By default the homepage's (home.rail). A page can pass its own list
  as `railItems` ({ label, target }); the case studies pass their sections,
  so the menu becomes the case's table of contents and the scroll-spy lights
  the section being read. `railBase: "/"` instead makes the items plain links
  back to the homepage's sections, with `railActive` naming the lit one.

  PROGRESS. `railProgress` puts the case study's reading progress (the "23%"
  pill, scripts/v4-progress.js) at the top of the menu.
#}
<div class="v4-rail-track">
  <nav class="v4-rail" aria-label="Page">
    {%- if railProgress %}
    <span class="v4-case__progress v4-rail__progress" data-read-progress aria-hidden="true">0%</span>
    {%- endif %}
    <ul class="v4-rail__list">
      {%- for item in (railItems or home.rail) %}
      <li>
        {%- set on = (item.target == railActive) if railActive else loop.first %}
        <a class="v4-rail__item{% if on %} is-active{% endif %}" href="{{ railBase or '' }}#{{ item.target }}"{% if not railBase %} data-rail-target="{{ item.target }}"{% endif %}{% if on %} aria-current="{{ 'page' if railBase else 'true' }}"{% endif %}>
          <span class="v4-rail__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          {{ item.label }}
        </a>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </nav>
</div>
